# Translation source and build scripts live in Source/; only the compiled assembly ships.
# .claude/ excludes session worktrees, which have already landed inside a mod folder once.
#
# Two separate reasons to have this file, and only the first is about git:
#
#   - The monorepo's own .gitignore covers all of this, but `git subtree split` exports this
#     folder alone. The root's rules do not travel with it.
#   - Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's
#     target directory as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in the
#     published folder is published. That is what `Mod/` is for: the junction points there,
#     and everything else in this folder - Art/, the docs, this file - stays out of reach by
#     construction.

# Build intermediates.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings: each worktree is a full copy of the
# monorepo, and they are never shared.
.claude/

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# System.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

node_modules/
package-lock.json
package.json
.worktrees/

# DDS textures: not tracked
*.dds

# Scratch stdout/stderr of the Pickle wrapper launches; the durable record is tests/Pickle/Evidence/
tests/Pickle/core-en-*.log

# Raw Pickle reports stay on disk; one text summary per run goes in docs/runs/
tests/Pickle/Evidence/

# Old-style report folders: raw evidence stays under tests/Pickle/Evidence/ (ignored); history is docs/runs/
tests/pickle-run-*/
tests/audit-*/
tests/workflow-*audit*/
tests/translation-validation-*/
